From: Chris Wiggins <chris@cwiggs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ec/google/chromeec: Allow After-G3 sync without CFR

The After-G3 synchronization was introduced by MrChromebox commit
bb60ab176789 ("ec/google/chromeec: Add support for After G3 State"). Its
option lookup already falls back to CONFIG_MAINBOARD_POWER_FAILURE_STATE
when no option backend is available, so it does not require CFR and can
provide a static policy for payloads such as Heads.

Link: https://github.com/MrChromebox/coreboot/commit/bb60ab176789c7339baff7eaa829d93b66789c45
Signed-off-by: Chris Wiggins <chris@cwiggs.com>
---
 src/ec/google/chromeec/Kconfig | 9 ++++-----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ec/google/chromeec/Kconfig b/src/ec/google/chromeec/Kconfig
--- a/src/ec/google/chromeec/Kconfig
+++ b/src/ec/google/chromeec/Kconfig
@@ -202,14 +202,13 @@ config EC_GOOGLE_CHROMEEC_INCLUDE_SSFC_IN_FW_CONFIG
 
 config EC_GOOGLE_CHROMEEC_AFTER_G3_STATE
-	bool "Enable syncing ChromeEC After G3 State with CFR at boot"
+	bool "Enable syncing ChromeEC After G3 State at boot"
-	depends on DRIVERS_OPTION_CFR_ENABLED
 	help
-	  Enable syncing ChromeEC After G3 State with CFR at boot via host
-	  command, otherwise ChromeEC default compiled after G3 behavior
+	  Enable syncing ChromeEC After G3 State with the power failure option
+	  via host command, otherwise ChromeEC default compiled after G3 behavior
 	  (usually "Previous State") will override coreboot after G3
 	  configuration.
 
-	  After G3 State is synced from existing coreboot CFR:
+	  After G3 State is synced from the coreboot option:
 	    "Restore AC power after loss"
 
 	  This option has no effect if ChromeEC running image does not support
-- 
2.39.5
